From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomas Mihalicka <tomas@mihalicka.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Put storage and the provider behind ports

The payment service was wired to the file store and to the HTTP
provider client. Its signature named a transport, its errors came from
the log file module, and no other store or provider could stand behind
it.

Introduce two ports, PaymentStore and PaymentProvider, along with the
types that cross them, StoreError and ChargeRequest. The service and
the HTTP layer now depend only on the ports. FileStore and
ProviderClient implement them, and main is the one place that picks
the adapters. Behaviour is unchanged.

Areas: system-design
